@startuml
title lists-service v1 - Implemented logical data model

hide methods
hide stereotypes
skinparam shadowing false

note as StatusNote
  IMPLEMENTED LOGICAL MODEL
  Todoist remains the list/task system of record.
  Loops are Lists-owned PostgreSQL records, verified on a disposable database.
  Provider fields were checked against Todoist API v1.
  Tenant catalogue/project mapping has local automated evidence;
  multitenant live-provider and deployment evidence remain pending.
end note

entity "Todoist Project / TaskList" as Project {
  * id : string <<provider identity>>
  --
  name : string
  childOrder : integer
  inboxProject : boolean
}

entity "Todoist Task / ShoppingListItem" as Item {
  * id : string <<provider identity>>
  --
  * projectId : string <<provider reference>>
  * content : string
  description : string [0..1]
  * isCompleted : boolean
  childOrder : integer
  priority : integer 1..4 [TaskListTask, optional]
  createdAt : timestamp [0..1]
  completedAt : timestamp [0..1]
}

entity "Runtime Configuration" as Configuration {
  shoppingTodoistProjectId : string [preferred]
  --
  shoppingTodoistProjectName : string [fallback]
  * restApiTokenSecretReference : secret reference
  * life2JwtSigningKeySecretReference : secret reference
  * servicePrincipalAccountId : identifier
  * tenantCatalogSecretReference : secret reference
  alexaSkillId : string [only after real skill creation]
  * releaseGitCommit : sha1
  restActiveVersion : positive integer [0..1]
  alexaActiveVersion : positive integer [0..1]
  * logLevel : string
  * completedLookbackDays : integer (1..90)
}

entity "Tenant Todoist connection catalogue entry" as Connection {
  * accountId : Life2 tenant identifier
  --
  * tokenSecretRef : secret reference
  shoppingProjectId : provider identity [xor]
  shoppingProjectName : string [xor]
}

entity "Protected tenant Todoist token" as TenantToken {
  * secretReference : identifier
  --
  tokenValue : secret <<never in catalogue>>
}

entity "Workspace search hit" as SearchHit {
  * transient resource identity
  --
  type, title, subtitle
  score
  allowlisted route target
}

entity "Loop" as Loop {
  * id : uuid
  --
  * accountId : Life2 tenant identifier
  * title : varchar(160)
  description : varchar(2000) [0..1]
  * priority : high | medium | low
  * outcome : varchar(2000)
  dueDate : date [0..1]
  * status : open | closed
  * createdBySub, updatedBySub : Life2 user identifier
  createdAt, updatedAt, closedAt : timestamp
}

entity "Loop related record" as LoopReference {
  * loopId : uuid
  * recordKind : task | appointment | email | document | entity | other
  * recordId : opaque source identifier
  --
  label : source-faithful display label
  ordinal : small integer
}

entity "Lists schema migration" as Migration {
  * name : varchar(255)
  --
  appliedAt : timestamptz
}

Project ||--o{ Item : contains
Connection ..> Project : token exposes existing lists
Connection ||--|| TenantToken : references
Configuration ..> Connection : loads catalogue
Configuration ..> Project : selects tenant Shopping project
Project ||..o{ SearchHit : projected on demand
Item ||..o{ SearchHit : active tasks projected on demand
Loop ||--o{ LoopReference : brings together record references
Migration ..> Loop : 001_loops.sql creates

note right of Configuration
  Stores references and identifiers only.
  Secret values are retrieved at runtime from
  AWS Secrets Manager or local read-only files.
  The name-only Shopping project is created when absent.
  Task Lists enumerates projects through the token selected
  exclusively by the verified JWT accountId.
  This is configuration, not persisted
  application-domain data.
  Published Lambda versions and aliases provide
  release rollback; Todoist data is not copied.
  The public heartbeat selects only the deployment-bound
  Shopping account and performs a bounded provider read;
  it never exposes this identifier or provider details.
end note

note bottom of Connection
  The catalogue contains no token values and rejects duplicate
  accountId entries. A missing entry reports not_connected.
  Browser onboarding and disconnect are unavailable.
end note

note bottom of Item
  GET /v1/items.pdf reads active tasks and renders a transient
  tenant Shopping snapshot. No PDF or list entity is persisted.
  PATCH /v1/items/:itemId changes content only after the item is
  resolved from the configured Shopping project.
end note

note bottom of SearchHit
  Search hits are transient and tenant-scoped.
  No additional database or search index is introduced.
end note

note bottom of Loop
  Lists owns these PostgreSQL rows. Related source records remain
  in their owning services and are never copied. A Plaud-aware agent
  uses Life2 MCP; Lists has no direct Plaud provider dependency.
end note

note bottom of Migration
  The first production database is owned by lists_migrator.
  Default table grants give lists_runtime DML and lists_backup
  SELECT only. lists_restore has no production database CONNECT;
  its cluster CREATEDB grant is used only for a scratch restore.
  Credentials live in separate root-only files, outside this model.
end note

StatusNote .. Item

entity "Todoist Comment" as Comment {
  * id : string <<provider identity>>
  --
  taskId : string
  content : string
}
Item ||--o{ Comment : "task_id; provider owned"
note right of Comment
UUID request keys pass through to Todoist.
No Lists-owned comment or replay table is added.
end note
@enduml
